[{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>The diagram below shows a sector of a circle, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. By considering trigonometric ratios, show that as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\to0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin\\theta\\approx\\tan\\theta\\approx\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.19/questions/assets/diagrams/219-q1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sin\\theta=\\frac hr\\Rightarrow h=r\\sin\\theta\\text{ and }\\tan\\theta=\\frac hy\\Rightarrow h=y\\tan\\theta\\text{ so }r\\sin\\theta=y\\tan\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\to0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\\to r\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\to r\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\\sin\\theta\\approx r\\tan\\theta\\approx r\\theta\\Rightarrow\\sin\\theta\\approx\\tan\\theta\\approx\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Show that if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin\\theta\\approx\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\to0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta\\approx1-\\frac{\\theta^2}2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos2x=1-2\\sin^2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac\\theta2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta=1-2\\sin^2(\\frac\\theta2)\\approx1-2(\\frac\\theta2)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta\\approx1-\\frac{\\theta^2}2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is small, find an approximation for the following:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos6\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan\\theta-2\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\tan3\\theta+\\cos3\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\times\\theta=\\theta^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1-\\frac{\\theta^2}2-1=-\\frac{\\theta^2}2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1-\\frac{(6\\theta)^2}2=1-18\\theta^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta-2\\theta=-\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\times3\\theta+1-\\frac{(3\\theta)^2}2=3\\theta^2+1-\\frac92\\theta^2=1-\\frac32\\theta^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is small enough for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to be ignored, find an approximation for the following:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\theta\\tan\\theta}{1-\\cos\\theta}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta\\cos3\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos^2\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\theta^2\\sin\\theta}{1-\\cos2\\theta}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\cos8\\theta-\\cos4\\theta}{\\sin8\\theta-\\sin4\\theta}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{1-\\cos2\\theta}{6\\tan\\theta}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\theta^2}{1-1-\\frac{\\theta^2}2}=\\frac{\\theta^2}{\\frac{\\theta^2}2}=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1-\\frac{\\theta^2}2)(1-\\frac{(3\\theta)^2}2)=1-\\frac{\\theta^2}2-\\frac{9\\theta^2}2+\\frac{9\\theta^4}4=1-5\\theta^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1-\\frac{\\theta^2}2)(1-\\frac{\\theta^2}2)\\approx1-\\theta^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta^2+1-\\theta^2=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\theta^3}{1-(1-\\frac{(2\\theta)^2}2)}=\\frac{\\theta^3}{2\\theta^2}=\\frac12\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{1-\\frac{(8\\theta)^2}2-(1-\\frac{(4\\theta)^2}2)}{8\\theta-4\\theta}=\\frac{1-32\\theta^2-1+8\\theta^2}{4\\theta}=\\frac{-24\\theta^2}{4\\theta}=-6\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">g)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{1-(1-\\frac{(2\\theta)^2}2)}{6\\theta}=\\frac{2\\theta^2}{6\\theta}=\\frac13\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q5","number":5,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find an approximation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos0.4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> by using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=0.1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and small angle approximations.</p></li><li><p>Find the percentage error of your approximation.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos4\\theta\\approx1-\\frac{(4\\theta)^2}2\\approx1-8\\theta^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos0.4\\approx1-8(0.1)^2\\approx1-0.08\\approx0.92\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos0.4=0.9210610\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Percentage error is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{0.0010610\\ldots}{0.9210610\\ldots}\\times100=0.115\\%\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is small, use the standard small angle approximations for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> find:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cot2\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cot4\\theta-\\operatorname{cosec}2\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac\\theta{\\sin\\theta}\\approx\\frac\\theta\\theta\\approx1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{\\tan2\\theta}\\approx\\frac1{2\\theta}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{\\tan4\\theta}-\\frac1{\\sin2\\theta}\\approx\\frac1{4\\theta}-\\frac1{2\\theta}=-\\frac1{4\\theta}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q7","number":7,"question":"<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\sec x(\\sin x+\\cos x)\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>By using the small angle approximations for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\\approx1+x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>By using the small angle approximation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and an alternative approximation, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos x\\approx1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\\approx1+x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the percentage error when approximating <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(0.1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\sin x+\\cos x}{\\cos x}=\\tan x+1\\approx x+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{x+1}1\\approx x+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\sin0.1+\\cos0.1}{\\cos0.1}\\approx1.1\\text{ and }\\frac{\\sin0.1+\\cos0.1}{\\cos0.1}=1.100335\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Percentage error is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{0.000335\\ldots}{1.100335\\ldots}\\times100=0.0304\\%\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q8","number":8,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is small, show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-2+\\cos\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta\\approx-1+\\frac12\\theta^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence find an approximate solution to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-2+\\cos\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=4\\tan\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-2+1-\\frac{\\theta^2}2+\\theta^2\\approx-1+\\frac12\\theta^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-1+\\tfrac12\\theta^2\\approx4\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\theta^2-4\\theta-1=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has solutions <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\\pm3\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\approx-0.243\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\approx8.24\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. But <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is small so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\approx-0.243\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>Given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is small, find the approximate solution to</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{1-\\cos(\\frac1{10}x)}{\\sin x}=\\frac15-\\tan x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{1-(1-\\frac{(0.1x)^2}2)}x\\approx\\frac{x^2/200}x\\approx\\frac1{200}x\\text{ and }\\frac15-x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac1{200}x\\approx\\frac15-x\\text{ so }x\\approx\\frac{40}{201}\\approx0.199\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q10","number":10,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find, for small values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, an approximation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=2+4\\tan\\frac x2-8\\sin\\frac x3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Use your result in part a) to sketch an approximation for the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-0.2\\leq x\\leq0.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Include the start and end coordinates in your sketch.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\\approx2+4\\times\\frac x2-8\\times\\frac x3\\approx2-\\frac23x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.19/solutions/assets/diagrams/219-s10b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>Given that the root of the equation is small, find the single solution to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x-\\frac14+\\cos x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is small <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos x\\approx1-\\frac{x^2}2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2x-\\tfrac14+1-\\tfrac{x^2}2=0\\Rightarrow2x+\\tfrac34-\\tfrac{x^2}2=0\\Rightarrow\\tfrac{x^2}2-2x-\\tfrac34=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=2\\pm\\sqrt{\\tfrac{11}2}\\text{ so }x\\approx-0.345\\text{ or }x\\approx4.35\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is small <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\approx-0.345\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>Given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is small enough for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to be ignored, by approximating <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan x+\\tan x\\cos4x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int_0^{0.3}\\sqrt[3]{\\tan x(1+\\cos4x)}\\,dx\\approx0.190\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x+x(1-\\tfrac{(4x)^2}2)\\approx x+x(1-8x^2)\\approx x+x-8x^3\\approx2x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int_0^{0.3}(2x)^{1/3}\\,dx =\\int_0^{0.3}2^{1/3}x^{1/3}\\,dx=[2^{1/3}\\times\\tfrac34x^{4/3}]_0^{0.3}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =(0.60249\\ldots)-(0)=0.189772\\ldots\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Which is approximately 0.190 as req.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q13","number":13,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is small, find an approximation to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta-\\cos2\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lim_{\\theta\\to0}\\frac{\\cos\\theta-\\cos2\\theta}{\\theta^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1-\\frac{\\theta^2}2-(1-\\frac{(2\\theta)^2}2)=1-\\frac{\\theta^2}2-1+\\frac{4\\theta^2}2=-\\frac{\\theta^2}2+2\\theta^2=\\frac32\\theta^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lim_{\\theta\\to0}\\frac{\\cos\\theta-\\cos2\\theta}{\\theta^2}=\\lim_{\\theta\\to0}\\frac{\\frac32\\theta^2}{\\theta^2}=\\lim_{\\theta\\to0}\\frac32=\\frac32\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>Find these limits:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\cos h-1}h\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\sin h}h\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\cos h-1}h=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{1-\\frac{h^2}2-1}h=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{-\\frac{h^2}2}h=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac h2=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\sin h}h=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac hh=\\lim_{h\\to0}1=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q15","number":15,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q15-Q18: Differentiation from First Principles and Compound Angle Formulae</strong> Differentiate from first principles the following functions by using knowledge about small angle approximations:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(\\theta)=\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(\\theta)=\\cos\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(\\theta)=\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dy}{d\\theta} =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\sin(\\theta+h)-\\sin\\theta}h=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\sin\\theta\\cos h+\\sin h\\cos\\theta-\\sin\\theta}h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\sin\\theta(\\cos h-1)+\\cos\\theta(\\sin h)}h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\sin\\theta(1-\\frac{h^2}2-1)+\\cos\\theta(h)}h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{-\\frac12h^2\\sin\\theta+h\\cos\\theta}h=\\lim_{h\\to0}(-\\tfrac12h\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta)=\\cos\\theta\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(\\theta)=\\cos\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dy}{d\\theta} =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\cos(\\theta+h)-\\cos\\theta}h=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\cos\\theta\\cos h-\\sin h\\sin\\theta-\\cos\\theta}h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\cos\\theta(\\cos h-1)-\\sin\\theta(\\sin h)}h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\cos\\theta(1-\\frac{h^2}2-1)-\\sin\\theta(h)}h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{-\\frac12h^2\\cos\\theta-h\\sin\\theta}h=\\lim_{h\\to0}(-\\tfrac12h\\cos\\theta-\\sin\\theta)=-\\sin\\theta\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>Using differentiation from first principles, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\cos(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find the exact value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(\\frac\\pi3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(\\tfrac\\pi3)=\\cos\\tfrac\\pi3=\\tfrac12,\\quad\\mathrm f(\\tfrac\\pi3+h)=\\cos(\\tfrac\\pi3+h)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dy}{d\\theta} =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\cos(\\frac\\pi3+h)-\\frac12}h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\cos\\frac\\pi3\\cos h-\\sin\\frac\\pi3\\sin h-\\frac12}h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\frac12\\cos h-\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\sin h-\\frac12}h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\frac12(\\cos h-1)-\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\sin h}h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\frac12(1-\\frac{h^2}2-1)-\\frac{\\sqrt3}2h}h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{-\\frac14h^2-\\frac{\\sqrt3}2h}h=\\lim_{h\\to0}(-\\tfrac14h-\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}2)=-\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}2\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q17","number":17,"question":"<p>Prove, using differentiation from first principles, that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac d{dx}(\\tan\\theta)=\\sec^2\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(\\theta)=\\tan\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dy}{d\\theta} =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\tan(\\theta+h)-\\tan\\theta}h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\frac{\\sin(\\theta+h)}{\\cos(\\theta+h)}-\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}}h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\frac{\\sin(\\theta+h)\\cos\\theta-\\cos(\\theta+h)\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta\\cos(\\theta+h)}}h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\sin(\\theta+h)\\cos\\theta-\\cos(\\theta+h)\\sin\\theta}{h\\cos\\theta\\cos(\\theta+h)}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Using the compound angle formula:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\sin(\\theta+h-\\theta)}{h\\cos\\theta\\cos(\\theta+h)}=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\sin h}{h\\cos\\theta\\cos(\\theta+h)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>For small angles:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac h{h\\cos\\theta\\cos(\\theta+h)}=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac1{\\cos\\theta\\cos(\\theta+h)}=\\frac1{\\cos^2\\theta}=\\sec^2\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q18","number":18,"question":"<p>Prove, using differentiation from first principles, that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac d{dx}(\\sec\\theta)=\\sec\\theta\\tan\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(\\theta)=\\sec\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dy}{d\\theta} =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\frac1{\\cos(\\theta+h)}-\\frac1{\\cos\\theta}}h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac1h\\left[\\frac1{\\cos(\\theta+h)}-\\frac1{\\cos\\theta}\\right]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac1h\\left[\\frac{\\cos\\theta-\\cos(\\theta+h)}{\\cos(\\theta+h)\\cos\\theta}\\right]\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Using the compound angle formula:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac1h\\left[\\frac{\\cos\\theta-\\cos\\theta\\cos h+\\sin\\theta\\sin h}{\\cos(\\theta+h)\\cos h}\\right]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac1h\\left[\\frac{\\cos\\theta(1-\\cos h)+\\sin\\theta\\sin h}{\\cos(\\theta+h)\\cos\\theta}\\right]\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>For small angles:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac1h\\left[\\frac{\\cos\\theta(1-1+\\frac12h^2)+h\\sin\\theta}{\\cos(\\theta+h)\\cos\\theta}\\right]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\frac12h\\cos\\theta+\\sin\\theta}{\\cos(\\theta+h)\\cos\\theta}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta}=\\sec\\theta\\tan\\theta\\text{ as req.}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q19","number":19,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q19-Q20: Binomial Series</strong></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the first three terms, in ascending powers of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of the binomial expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1-8x)^{1/2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence, for small values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin2x+\\sqrt{\\cos4x}\\approx a+bx+cx^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are constants to be found and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is small enough for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to be ignored.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1-8x)^{1/2}\\approx1+\\tfrac12(-8x)+\\tfrac12(\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac12)(-8x)^2\\approx1-4x-8x^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\sin2x+\\sqrt{\\cos4x} \\approx2x+(1-\\tfrac{(4x)^2}2)^{1/2}\\approx2x+(1-8x^2)^{1/2}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Sub <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> into result from before: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1-4x^2-8x^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\approx2x+(1-8x^2)^{1/2}\\approx2x+1-4x^2-8x^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Ignoring <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> terms <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\approx1+2x-4x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q20","number":20,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the first two terms, in ascending powers of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of the binomial expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1-\\frac12x^2)^{1/3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence find an approximation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\int_0^{0.2}\\sqrt[3]{\\cos x}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answer to 4 decimal places.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1-\\tfrac12x^2)^{1/3}\\approx1+\\tfrac13(-\\tfrac12x^2)\\approx1-\\tfrac16x^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int_0^{0.2}(\\cos x)^{1/3}\\,dx \\approx\\int_0^{0.2}(1-\\tfrac12x^2)^{1/3}\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n \\approx\\int_0^{0.2}(1-\\tfrac16x^2)\\,dx\\approx[x-\\tfrac1{18}x^3]_0^{0.2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n \\approx(0.199556)-(0)=0.1996\\text{ (4 dp)}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q21","number":21,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q21-Q22: Differentiation of Trigonometric Functions</strong> Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at the origin of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac12\\tan4y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> by:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>using Calculus</p></li><li><p>using a small angle approximation and Calculus</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dx}{dy}=2\\sec^24y=\\frac2{\\cos^24y}\\Rightarrow\\left.\\frac{dx}{dy}\\right|_{y=0}=2\\text{ so }\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(0,0)}=\\tfrac12\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\tfrac12\\tan4y\\approx\\tfrac12\\times4y\\text{ so }x\\approx2y\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dx}{dy}\\right|_{(0,0)}=2\\Rightarrow\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(0,0)}=\\tfrac12\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q22","number":22,"question":"<p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3\\cos16y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;y&lt;\\frac\\pi2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> by:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>using Calculus</p></li><li><p>using a small angle approximation and Calculus</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"16y=\\frac\\pi2\\Rightarrow y=\\frac\\pi{32}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dx}{dy}=-48\\sin16y\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dx}{dy}\\right|_{y=\\pi/32}=-48\\text{ so }\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\tfrac1{48}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3\\cos16y\\approx3(1-\\tfrac{(16y)^2}2)\\approx3-384y^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\approx3-384y^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\approx\\frac\\pi{32}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dx}{dy}=-768y\\Rightarrow\\left.\\frac{dx}{dy}\\right|_{y=\\pi/32}=-24\\pi\\text{ so }\\frac{dy}{dx}\\approx-\\tfrac1{24\\pi}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q23","number":23,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q23-Q24: Newton-Raphson Method</strong> Given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is small, find an approximate solution giving your answers to 3 significant figures for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12-x-\\sin2x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>by using small angle approximation</p></li><li><p>by using a Newton-Raphson approximation starting at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_0=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12-x-2x\\approx0\\Rightarrow3x\\approx\\frac12\\Rightarrow x\\approx\\frac16\\approx0.167\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac12-x-\\sin2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)=1-2\\cos2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=x_n-\\frac{\\frac12-x_n-\\sin2x_n}{-1-2\\cos2x_n}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_0=\\frac16\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=0.16879\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2=0.16879\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\approx0.169\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.19-q24","number":24,"question":"<p>Given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is small, find an approximate solution giving your answers to 3 significant figures for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2+5x+\\sin x=\\cos x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>by using small angle approximation</p></li><li><p>by using a Newton-Raphson approximation starting at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_0=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2+5x+x\\approx1-\\tfrac{x^2}2\\Rightarrow\\tfrac{x^2}2+6x+1\\approx0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x\\approx-0.169\\text{ or }x\\approx-11.8\\text{ but }x\\text{ is small so }x\\approx-0.169\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=2+5x+\\sin x-\\cos x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)=5+\\cos x+\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=x_n-\\frac{2+5x_n+\\sin x_n-\\cos x_n}{5+\\cos x_n+\\sin x_n}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_0=-\\frac16\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=-0.1691798\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2=-0.169180\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\approx-0.169\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]}]